/*
 * A random NPC fisher arrives on the beach and fishes nearby. They can slowly get drunk over the course of the session, making them more belligerent. If you catch
 * something while they're drunk, they might try to take it from you.
 */
:: Fishing Beach Fisher Arrive
<<generate1>><<saveNPC 0 "fishing_beach_npc_fisher">><<person1>>
<<set $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.phase to "fishing">>
<<set $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.age to 0>>
<<set $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.drunk to 0>>
<<fishingLocationDescription "beach">>
<br><br>

Another fisher, a <<person>>, walks down to the shore and sets up a short distance away.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Beach Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Beach Fisher Tips Offer
<<loadNPC 0 "fishing_beach_npc_fisher">><<person1>>
<<set $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.tipGiven to true>>

<<switch random(1, 3)>>
	<<case 1>>
		The <<person>> watches you for a moment, then takes a few steps toward you. "Hey, do you want some help? You look like you're fighting the fish more than you need to."
	<<case 2>>
		The <<person>> reels in, pauses, then adjusts something on <<his>> setup before casting again. After a moment <<he>> glances over. "I know this spot fairly well. Happy to share what I know, if you want."
	<<case 3>>
		The <<person>> reels in and checks <<his>> bait carefully, then glances over towards you. "How are you getting on?" <<He>> asks. "I know a couple of tricks for this spot, if you want to hear them."
<</switch>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Sure|Fishing Beach Fisher Tips]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[No thanks|Fishing Beach Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Beach Fisher Tips
<<switch random(1, 3)>>
	<<case 1>>
		The <<person>> demonstrates a few casts, pointing out where <<he>> aims and how <<he>> adjusts the tension as the line settles.
	<<case 2>>
		The <<person>> crouches near the waterline and points to where the sand drops off, explaining where the fish tend to run.
	<<case 3>>
		The <<person>> shows you how <<he>> positions <<his>> hands on the rod before casting, watching where the line lands and adjusting.
<</switch>>

After a while <<he>> turns back to <<his>> own rod, apparently satisfied.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Beach Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Beach Fisher Leave Night
<<loadNPC 0 "fishing_beach_npc_fisher">><<person1>>
<<clearNPC "fishing_beach_npc_fisher">>
<<set $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.phase to "finished">>

The <<person>> glances up at the darkening sky and starts to pack up <<his>> fishing gear. "I'm not a fan of night fishing around these parts. You should head home too."
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Beach Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Beach Fisher Leave Weather
<<loadNPC 0 "fishing_beach_npc_fisher">><<person1>>
<<clearNPC "fishing_beach_npc_fisher">>
<<set $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.phase to "finished">>

The <<person>> looks up as the weather begins to turn rough, then begins to pack up <<his>> fishing gear. "The weather is turning, I'm going to head home before it gets any worse. You should head out too."
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Beach Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Beach Events [widget]
<<widget "fishingBeachFisherAmbient">>
	<<loadNPC 0 "fishing_beach_npc_fisher">><<person1>>
	<<set $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.age += 1>>
	<<cleareventpool>>

	<<addinlineevent 1>>
		The <<person>> reels in, checks the empty hook, and lets out a quiet sigh before casting back out.
	<</addinlineevent>>
	<<addinlineevent 5>>
		The <<person>> reels in, re-baits the hook, and casts back out.
	<</addinlineevent>>
	<<addinlineevent 1>>
		The <<person>> reels in, takes a small fish off the hook and tosses it back before casting back out.
	<</addinlineevent>>
	<<addinlineevent 1>>
		The <<person>> reels in, takes a small fish off the hook and stores it in <<his>> bag before casting back out.
	<</addinlineevent>>
	<<addinlineevent 1>>
		The <<person>> picks a clump of seaweed off <<his>> line and casts back out.
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<if $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.drunk gte 3>>
		<<addinlineevent 15>>
			The <<person1>><<person>> sways slightly on <<his>> feet, rod dipping toward the water.
		<</addinlineevent>>
		<<addinlineevent 1>>
			The <<person>> reels in, squints at the hook, and mutters something under <<his>> breath before casting sloppily back out.
		<</addinlineevent>>
		<<addinlineevent 1>>
			The <<person>> tugs <<his>> line free from a snag with more force than necessary, nearly losing <<his>> footing.
		<</addinlineevent>>
		<<addinlineevent 1>>
			The <<person>> fumbles with the bait for a moment before managing to hook it, then casts back out with a grunt.
		<</addinlineevent>>
		<<addinlineevent 4>>
			The <<person>> glances over at you, eyes a little unfocused. <<He>> gives you a slow, lopsided smile before turning back to <<his>> rod.
		<</addinlineevent>>
		<<addinlineevent 2>>
			The <<person>> loses <<his>> balance for a moment, stumbling in the sand before catching <<himself>>. <<He>> laughs softly to <<himself>>.
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<<else>>
		<<addinlineevent 15>>
			The <<person>> stands a few paces away, quiet and focused on <<his>> line.
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>

	<<addinlineevent 1>>
		The <<person>> reaches into <<his>> bag, pulls out a flask, and takes a long drink before tucking it away.
		<<set $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.drunk += 1>>
	<</addinlineevent>>
	<<addinlineevent 1>>
		The <<person>> pulls out a flask and drinks from it, then goes back to <<his>> rod.
		<<set $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.drunk += 1>>
	<</addinlineevent>>

	<<if $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.age gte 4>>
		<<addinlineevent 7>>
			<<set $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.age to 0>>
			The <<person>> suddenly braces, struggling with the line as <<his>> rod bends around. After a tense moment, <<he>> reels in and pulls out a fish with a satisfied grunt. <<He>> holds it up briefly before unhooking it and dropping it in <<his>> cooler.
		<</addinlineevent>>
		<<addinlineevent 12>>
			<<set $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.age to 0>>
			The <<person>> suddenly braces, fighting with the line as it pulls <<his>> rod around. Then <<he>> jolts back as whatever was on the line escapes.
			<<if $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.drunk gte 3>>
				<<He>> swears loudly, fumbling with <<his>> line before eventually getting it hooked and cast back out.
			<<else>>
				With a sigh, <<he>> re-hooks <<his>> line and casts back out.
			<</if>>
		<</addinlineevent>>
	<</if>>
	<<runeventpool>>
<</widget>>


:: Fishing Beach Fisher Give Fish
The <<person>> snatches it from your hands and staggers off, muttering about "respekt" and "my spot." 
<br><br>

<<clearNPC "fishing_beach_npc_fisher">>
<<set $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.phase to "finished">>
<<link [[Next|Fishing Beach Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Beach Fisher Give Fish Attack
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"But I caught it... it's mine."
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Not a chance. Get your own."
<<else>>
	"No. I caught it."
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<He>> narrows <<his>> eyes. "I tend to take what I want," <<he>> says as <<he>> strides towards you.
<br><br>

<<link [[Fight|Fishing Beach Fisher Molestation]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>><</link>>


:: Fishing Beach Fisher Molestation
<<if $molestationstart is 1>>
	<<run stopFishingProp()>>
	<<set $molestationstart to 0>>
	<<controlloss>>
	<<violence 1>>
	<<neutral 1>>
	<<molested>>
	<<set $enemyno to 1>>
	<<maninit>>
<</if>>

<<effects>>
<<effectsman>>
<<alarmstate>>
<<man>>
<<stateman>>
<br><br>

<<actionsman>>

<<if _combatend>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Fishing Beach Fisher Molestation Finish]]>><</link>></span>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Fishing Beach Fisher Molestation]]>><</link>></span>
<</if>>


:: Fishing Beach Fisher Molestation Finish
<<effects>>
<<clearNPC "fishing_beach_npc_fisher">>
<<set $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.phase to "finished">>

<<if $enemyarousal gte $enemyarousalmax>>
	<<ejaculation>>
	<<He>> shudders and pulls away, breathing hard. After a moment, <<he>> staggers up the beach and disappears over a dune.
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you get to your feet.
	<br><br>

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>
	<<link [[Return to fishing|Fishing Beach Wait]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<<elseif $enemyhealth lte 0>>
	<<He>> stumbles back, gasping. <<He>> looks at you for a moment, then turns and walks off down the beach.
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you gather yourself.
	<br><br>

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>
	<<tending_give>>
	<<link [[Return to fishing|Fishing Beach Wait]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<</if>>

<<widget "fishingWaitOrgasmBeachFisher">>
	<<loadNPC 0 "fishing_beach_npc_fisher">><<person1>>
	<<set _orgasmText to either("You dig the end of your rod into the sand to keep upright", "Your knees nearly buckle, your rod dragging furrows in the wet sand")>>
	<<orgasm>>
	<<= _orgasmText>> as your body convulses. As you steady yourself, you find the <<person>> watching you."Hell of a catch," <<he>> calls over, laughing. <<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>><<fameexhibitionism 10>>
<</widget>>


/* ========================== */
/* ===== Combat Widgets ===== */
/* ========================== */


:: Widgets Fishing Beach Fisher Molestation [widget]
<<widget "fishCombatBeachCaughtFisherDrunk">>
	<<run updateFishRecord($fishingHookedFish.type, $fishingHookedFish.size, "beach")>>
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<<run holdCaughtFish($fishingHookedFish.type)>>

	<<fishingCatchFishText "beach">>
	<br><br>

	<<loadNPC 0 "fishing_beach_npc_fisher">><<person1>>
	The <<person>> stares at your catch for a moment, eyes narrowing. <<He>> straightens up unsteadily and takes a step toward you. "That one's mine, I had a line right there. Hand it over."
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Give <<him>> the fish|Fishing Beach Fisher Give Fish]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Refuse|Fishing Beach Fisher Give Fish Attack]]>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatBeachOrgasmFisher">>
	<<loadNPC 0 "fishing_beach_npc_fisher">><<person1>>
	<<set _orgasmText to either("You dig the end of your rod into the sand to keep upright", "Your knees nearly buckle, your rod dragging furrows in the wet sand")>>
	<<orgasm>>
	<<= _orgasmText>> as your body convulses. The rod slips from your grip. By the time you recover, the line has gone slack and the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> is long gone. "Hell of a catch," the <<person>> calls over, laughing. <<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>><<fameexhibitionism 10>>
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Fishing Beach Wait]]>><</link>>
<</widget>>
